@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] crates-load-only-exports
Game crates MUST load only exported files (each asset's `.glb` and its declared outputs), never an asset's
`src/` or `asset.toml`, and MUST NOT depend on how an export was made. They MUST NOT name a region or
depend on how the world is split into regions: the world is tiles and an index.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] one-feature-per-crate
Each crate MUST be one feature, published as one Bevy plugin. That plugin MAY add private plugins for the
feature's parts; no other crate adds them. What several screens share lives in `screens`. A crate
MAY use another crate only for what that crate publishes for others (as the viewer uses `characters`),
never for its internals.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] stable-under-temporal-anti-aliasing
The world is drawn with temporal anti-aliasing, so what is drawn MUST NOT change from frame to frame in screen space
unless it moves in the world: no screen-space dither, stochastic transparency or crossfading visibility range (the
world crate makes any range abrupt and logs an error). Detail MUST swap whole primitives, as a tile's versions
swap whole. A vertex shader that moves geometry MUST write motion vectors that say how it moved, or say on
purpose that it stood still, as the wind's do. It MUST also draw the main pass no further than its prepass did (the
wind's `DEPTH_MARGIN`): the two passes are compiled apart, and a vertex a rounding error further fails the depth test
and leaves a hole showing the clear colour for a frame.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] nothing-appears-after-loading
The world MUST NOT show until all it draws is ready: its tiles, models and textures loaded and every pipeline made,
whichever way the camera looks. What loads with the world MUST hold the splash until it is ready (the world's
`Unready`, or a load the splash checks), and MUST be spawned, if hidden, so that it is drawn under it, as the
paraglider is, too small to see. The game logs any pipeline made once the world has loaded.
